> There are FAhAs for "front", "back", "right", and "left", but not for
> "side" in general, it seems. How would you express this location tense
>  as in "Buttons at side (There are buttons at the sides of the
> garment)" without "mlana"?
.skamyxatra

There's no general FAhA for "side," but a number of them come close.  Looking
at the list, I see:

  {ne'a} - next to, approximating
  {re'o} - adjacent to, touching, contacting
  {te'e} - bordering, edged by, edging up to
  {zo'a} - tangential to, passing by

Either "{re'o}" or "{te'e}" would probably be the best option in this case.

mu'omi'e .kamymecraijun.

